{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T12:48:50.481Z","ordinal":17130,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a101cf-6131-7320-99ca-7c5839fd9366","author":"/root/astra_ultra_final_judge","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/astra_ultra_final_judge\nPayload:\nNo remaining blocking measurement issue in the updated source.\n\nThe deferred restoration, exact-control validity, positive control, pixel-layout guards and warmed frustum queries address the identified defects.\n\nOne useful consistency check for the fresh report: compare the **Town-cell frustum sets** in `geometryInventory` and `cells`. The current nonempty check could pass because another object is visible even if the inventory’s Town-cell queries failed.\n\nZero removable cells supports only “no whole-cell removal opportunity found in these frozen views.” It establishes neither GPU submission counts nor potential savings elsewhere. I have not executed the updated build."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a101c3-e32d-7580-ba72-be0d3d17ace2","create_time":1791031730.481475}}}
