{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T12:55:32.170Z","ordinal":17203,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":173193029,"cached_input_tokens":170876800,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":420404,"reasoning_output_tokens":168027,"total_tokens":173613433},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":47646,"cached_input_tokens":47360,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":487,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":48133},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":33.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1791583131},"secondary":null,"credits":{"has_credits":true,"unlimited":false,"balance":"63618.8998305000"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"pro","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T12:55:32.181Z","ordinal":17204,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","turn_id":"01a101c3-e32d-7580-ba72-be0d3d17ace2","last_agent_message":"**Yes—geometry is a strong suspect, especially Marvin itself. But the GPU also spends substantial time on shading and repeated rendering passes.**\n\nThe latest native scene audit found:\n\n| Geometry inside the camera’s viewing volume | Base triangles |\n|---|---:|\n| Marvin and its attached geometry | **992,079** |\n| Crowd batches | 117,147 |\n| Town architecture | 109,424 |\n\nThese are mesh counts, **not confirmed GPU submissions**. Nevertheless, Marvin deserves investigation before reducing town detail.\n\nMy optimization plan, in priority order:\n\n1. **Attribute Marvin’s actual GPU cost.** Identify its draws in Xcode’s Metal capture, including shadow and ambient-occlusion passes. Investigate enclosed motors, electronics and internal surfaces. Remove geometry only when it cannot affect appearance across camera angles, articulation, shadows and reflections. Preserve exterior detail.\n\n2. **Reduce repeated geometry processing.** The earlier capture processed approximately 1.23 million primitives in both the main and ambient-occlusion preparation passes, plus roughly 1.7 million in each shadow pass. Investigate shared geometry, tighter shadow-caster selection and reusable static work.\n\n3. **Improve visibility filtering where measurements justify it.** We already spatially batch the town. At two tested street viewpoints, every in-frustum architecture cell contributed pixels; simply hiding whole cells would damage the image. Investigate smaller batches and conservative occlusion behind buildings, while retaining off-screen objects whose shadows remain visible.\n\n4. **Optimize ground, dust and ambient-occlusion shading.** These have measured GPU costs. Reduce redundant calculations, texture reads and transparent coverage while preserving the rendered result. Revisit previous unsuccessful experiments only with new evidence.\n\n5. **Check GPU scheduling and resource traffic.** Investigate unnecessary uploads, mipmap generation and dependencies between passes. Spare CPU cores cannot compensate for GPU work that misses the frame deadline.\n\nEach change gets a controlled comparison, image review and a measured GPU result. Final acceptance remains **ten-minute clear and storm drives on this M2**, full detail, actual presentation timing, and a target GPU P99 below **12.5 ms** for headroom.\n\nThe Astra Ultra judge reviewed this order and agreed—with the explicit caveat that Marvin’s large mesh count is an investigation target, not yet proof of the bottleneck. **Constant 60 FPS is still unproven.**","started_at":1791030977,"completed_at":1791032132,"duration_ms":1154889,"time_to_first_token_ms":7476}}
